# Implementation Report

These rules define the format of the implementation summary provided after each completed development task, ensuring concise and consistent reporting.

Guiding Principle:
Report only information that helps the developer understand what changed and what remains to be done.

After completing each implementation task, provide a concise report containing only the following sections.

## Implementation Summary

A short description (3–8 bullet points) of what was implemented.

## Files Modified

List:

* New files
* Modified files
* Deleted files (if any)

Include a one-line description of the purpose of each important file.

## Tests

Summarize:

* Tests added
* Tests executed
* Test results

## Design Changes

If the implementation required changes to the design:

* Describe the change.
* Identify the affected section of `design.md`.

Otherwise simply state:

> No design changes.

## Remaining TODOs

List any known limitations or follow-up work discovered during implementation.

If none:

> None.
